00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:21.740
Episode Five:
Opportunity

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:21.830
Don't you think we've gotten pretty good?

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:23.090
At what?

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.100
At controlling the Biancas, right?

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:26.430
Yeah, yeah!
Yeah, yeah!

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:29.440
I still get bewildered from time to time.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:32.040
You do go at your own pace, don't you, Shipon?

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:33.600
Hmph.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.350
Even if you say I go at my own pace...

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.310
What the, what the, what the...?

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:41.180
Absolute victory

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:41.340
Absolute victory

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:41.470
Absolute victory

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:41.640
Absolute victory

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:41.720
Absolute victory

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:41.840
Absolute victory

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:42.010
Absolute victory

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:42.180
Absolute victory

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:42.590
Absolute victory

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:42.970
Absolute victory

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:43.510
Absolute victory

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:44.100
Absolute victory

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:44.430
Absolute victory

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:46.090
Absolute victory?

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:48.120
What's with this?

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:53.060
I see... It's that season again, isn't it?

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.170
Starting today, your classes will be going into special training.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.250
The first thing up is the slalom.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:01.420
The slalom?

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:02.980
The slalom!

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:10.730
Why is Mr. Shirogane here?

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:10.910
Well, some of you may get

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:12.350
And he's enthusiastic, on top of that.

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:14.840
...but we'll begin after we explain the course.

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:26.890
Too slow!

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:30.430
Set your minimum speed to twelve kilometers per second.

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:32.850
I'm doing the best I can as is!

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:33.860
Put your speed up!

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:34.900
Whoa!

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:40.110
Next!

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.280
H-here I go!

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:49.190
Do you think your time will improve like that!?

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.810
I-I'm sorry!

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:54.310
What's THAT supposed to accomplish?

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:56.330
Oh, that's no good!

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.820
Your speed, increase your speed!

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:01.510
Be passionate! You've got to be passionate, you guys!

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:02.950
Fire!

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.630
What's wrong, that was sloppy.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:12.030
It was terrible, having to do that all of the sudden.

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:15.560
It's because it's completely different from what we did up until yesterday...

00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:17.870
Well, the athletic festival is coming up soon.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:19.410
The athletic festival?

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:21.780
That's right, the athletic festival!

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:24.150
The combined athletic festival competition...

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:25.420
...for all five great Foundations is soon!

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:27.270
You must be absolutely victorious!

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.080
Hmm...

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.090
So that's "absolute victory"

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:33.320
That's why you guys are going to put yourselves through the paces!

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:38.930
"Wisely and slow; they stumble that run fast."

00:04:33.990 --> 00:04:34.990
What!?

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:35.950
No whats!

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:37.960
Boo...

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:38.900
Hey now!

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.590
Shakespeare, King Lear.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:45.630
Having the Big Four as the executive committee truly gives me hope.

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:48.060
Is it going to be tough for the Stellvia to be victorious?

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:50.120
Please leave it to us.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:53.640
It looks like the Akapusu, which has no experience winning...

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:55.580
...is getting extremely fired up...

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:59.610
...and the Vision and the El Santo are aiming to recapture their supremacy.

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:02.810
And the Odyssey, which is aiming for a repeat victory...

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:05.760
...has gone so far as to make something like this.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:15.390
This year, a burning storm is coming to the Asteroid Belt once more.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:18.160
The combined athletic festival...

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:20.000
...where the five foundations compete with each other...

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:22.130
...to compare their abilities s about to begin.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:29.040
The prominent competition, astroball.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:31.640
The Odyssey is aiming for victory...

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.300
...and has prepared a great team this year, too.

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:39.090
Their victory song...

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:41.180
...will certainly resound on Mars three months from now.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:46.190
Miguel, that jerk.

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:51.040
There was once a time when astroball was considered the Stellvia's forte.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:55.290
I want you all to bring back our golden age.

00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:59.230
How much money and time can be allotted to us?

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:03.010
As long as you don't ask for too much, as much as you want.

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:06.630
Well, then, we'll be putting in our requests this week.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:12.990
The headmaster seems to be putting forth quite a bit of effort.

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:15.970
It looks like he would like to take part himself.

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:18.980
Even though it's an athletic festival for the students' sakes.

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:23.030
We don't know if we can use this year's preparatory students or not.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:25.710
They're too carefree.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:28.230
Well, then, what shall we do?

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:31.410
The Odyssey of Mars has gone so far as to send us a written challenge...

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:34.210
Shall we put some fighting spirit into the preparatory students?

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:35.520
Fighting spirit?

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:38.410
Like dangle a carrot in front of them or something?

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:40.150
That's it!

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:58.300
And what will that accomplish?

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:00.670
Even if you say that...

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:04.640
Aren't the regular students primarily competing in the athletic festival?

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:07.470
Preparatory students! Your attention, please!

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.310
Each of the competitions at the combined athletic festival...

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:13.680
...include skills that will be used during the Great Mission.

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:16.990
The athletic festival is a distinguished battle...

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:19.120
...where the Foundations compare their skills.

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:23.350
I'm sure the regular students get serious about this, but...

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:24.530
And about that!

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:26.560
The winners of each competition will be considered...

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:29.660
...for participation in the Great Mission.

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:30.900
What? Really?

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:35.350
And for astroball, one preparatory student will be chosen to participate.

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:36.330
Hmm.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:40.980
That student will be the teammate that we add to the Big Four.

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:43.010
Let's aim for victory together...

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:46.280
...and obtain the qualification to participate in the Great Mission!

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:48.650
Yeah! I'm going to do it!

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:51.370
You spoke well.

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:54.950
We were having problems with them not being serious enough.

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:59.520
It's unusual for you to not be able to urge them on, Mr. Shirogane.

00:08:00.070 --> 00:08:00.970
Well, yeah.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:07.960
The headmaster is urging us to bring back the golden age of astroball.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:09.580
I see...

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:10.280
Hm?

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:12.160
Mr. Shirogane?

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:19.180
Back then... if I hadn't gotten a red card...

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:23.870
...the golden age of the Stellvia might still be going.

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:26.330
They said 'astroball player'!

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:28.620
It's a shortcut to the Great Mission.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:30.520
All of the sudden, I'm enthusiastic about this.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:31.620
I won't lose.

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:34.220
All right, everyone, calm down.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:35.120
I'm done.

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:35.520
Eh?

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:43.680
What do you think? Isn't it quite pretty?

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:46.380
Shipon, you're good.

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:48.480
Really.

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:54.680
It's not just astroball.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:57.020
There are lots of other competitions.

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:59.580
Well, it's an athletic festival, so of course there are.

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:03.020
It says that fifty people can participate in the triangle math game.

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:04.060
It might be the one to go for.

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:06.830
But even if you win, aren't the points low?

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:09.380
Astroball really is the one, isn't it?

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:10.660
It looks like.

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:13.340
So it's going to be a fierce competition, is it?

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:15.460
Everyone's thinking the same thing.

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:19.070
Wow, I want to try to be in this one!

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:21.670
It says manipulator art.

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:25.240
It says that you put together a new program and paint a picture with it.

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:26.360
It looks like fun.

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:31.110
What? What? What?

00:09:31.190 --> 00:09:34.800
Shipon, with you around, my heart can be at ease...

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:35.290
Really...

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:37.660
Oh, Shipon, I love you, I love you, I love you!

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:40.290
The depressing season has come again.

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:42.060
You mean the athletic festival?

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:46.250
The students who are too enthusiastic increase my workload.

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:49.610
It can't be helped, Ren. It's the athletic festival, after all.

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:52.310
Don't push them too far, will you?

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:56.310
We won't. This isn't the teachers' athletic festival, after all.

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:59.150
Unfortunately, it's just as she says.

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:04.120
Which means you have to skillfully convey that regret to your students.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:09.930
Yeah. We're counting on you to care for the students, too.

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:12.130
Okay, Captain.

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:14.790
The Ora-avis Machine Bianca was designed...

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:17.940
...with customization in mind, and thus is able...

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:20.760
...to equip different types of units to make them more useful.

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:23.810
In this way, it is able to utilize all sorts of abilities.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:26.300
Allow me to stop explaining their virtues here.

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:28.640
Everyone, go and modify your machines...

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:30.030
...to suit the competition you're participating in.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:31.040
Yes, ma'am.

00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:35.050
With this, my machine will be ridiculously fast!

00:10:35.270 --> 00:10:37.850
The sensors, it's the accuracy of the sensors.

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:41.340
Wing, wing, combine!

00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:43.990
Fly through the skies...

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:45.790
Once you're pretty much finished...

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:48.050
...take a test flight and check the condition of your machine.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:49.660
Huh?

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:55.360
Why!?

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:59.110
It's too sensitive!

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:14.520
Why isn't it working right?

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:16.460
After you expanded your unit...

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:19.500
...did you change the settings on your machine's control program?

00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:20.430
Hmm?
Hmm?

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:22.370
The machine's control program!

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:27.000
Shipon.

00:11:27.030 --> 00:11:27.570
Huh?

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.540
Please help me.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:30.760
Huh? What?

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:32.900
Change the program on my Bianca.

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:34.460
I'm first!

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:35.680
Please.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:39.180
But I'm in the middle of my own work...!

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:40.100
Kouta...

00:11:41.140 --> 00:11:42.670
You're not going to customize yours?

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:45.970
Even if they say "Great Mission," it just doesn't jump out at me.

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:48.250
You have no enthusiasm for the athletic festival?

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:49.730
I'll support our side.

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:52.240
Oh, maybe I'll participate in the math game.

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:00.700
Shipon is impressive, as always.

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:04.440
For some reason, Shipon normally seems slow.

00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:05.800
But she's pretty good, isn't she?

00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:08.870
She's incredible at everything but flying skills, isn't she?

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:12.110
I wonder why she's only poor at flying skills?

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:15.060
It's mysterious...

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:17.950
Hmm!

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:20.450
So we will take that secret!

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:22.460
And solve it! Let's shed some light on it!

00:12:22.890 --> 00:12:24.980
The secret of the diamond in the rough!

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:27.140
Huh? Huh?

00:12:42.580 --> 00:12:44.450
Well, it isn't anything serious.

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:47.990
It doesn't need a compress, but just in case...

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:50.130
Jojo, what's wrong?

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:52.210
The special training was a bit...

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:53.600
Yeah, yeah...

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:56.530
Well, Jojo doesn't matter.

00:12:56.600 --> 00:12:57.540
What did you say!?

00:12:57.970 --> 00:12:59.160
Hmm? What's up?

00:12:59.650 --> 00:13:03.900
Could you show us the physical health data for Shima Katase?

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:05.520
Right, right, the data.

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:06.880
Hmm?

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:08.120
Why?

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:10.770
There's something about Shipon, er, I mean, Miss Katase...

00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:12.890
...that we're very interested in.

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:14.650
Very interested in?

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:15.550
Yes!
 Yes!

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:19.840
Oh...

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:21.360
This girl...

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:23.050
Hmm.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:23.760
Huh?
Huh?

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:27.670
But the school can't show the personal data...

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:30.040
...of any of its students to any of the other students.

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:31.790
Is that so?

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:33.250
That's stingy, you know?

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:38.160
But you can measure it yourself.

00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:44.810
Dai-chan, Arisa, I'm finished!

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:49.270
Thanks. In return, we'll customize your Bianca, Shipon.

00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:51.540
Huh? No, you don't have to...

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:54.130
No need to hold back, no need at all.

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:56.120
Umm...

00:14:00.430 --> 00:14:03.120
Today we're going to practice cross formation flying.

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:23.700
Hey!

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:25.110
I'm sorry!

00:14:26.020 --> 00:14:27.610
Katase! What are you doing!?

00:14:31.250 --> 00:14:32.760
I sure am slow.

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:37.380
Whenever we do anything new, I'm sure to fail.

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:38.930
Are you rushing?

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:41.230
I'm not even sure myself.

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:44.460
It isn't that Shipon is slow.

00:14:44.990 --> 00:14:46.720
Her response time is normal.

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:49.840
Then why is she that bad at controlling her machine?

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:52.710
Are you trying to take in all of the information?

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:55.150
I've reduced it quite a bit, but...

00:14:55.430 --> 00:14:57.680
There's no problem with her actual vision, either...

00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:59.820
...and there's nothing unusual about her blood pressure or pulse.

00:15:00.490 --> 00:15:02.110
It's not like she's nervous.

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:03.990
Then what is it?

00:15:04.560 --> 00:15:05.580
I don't know.

00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:11.540
Hey, have you ever felt it the way you wanted to feel it?

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:13.440
"Feel it"?

00:15:14.900 --> 00:15:19.280
You have to feel it. You have to feel like you're the center of the universe.

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:22.580
Is that what you do, Otoyama?

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:26.340
The coordinates that the data relays to you are relative values.

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:29.460
You have to make yourself the absolute value.

00:15:30.270 --> 00:15:31.520
The absolute value?

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:34.060
Oh, that's right.

00:15:35.350 --> 00:15:36.090
Would you like some?

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:38.140
I'll take some.

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:50.110
Today's class will be the astroball player selection tryouts.

00:15:50.660 --> 00:15:52.070
So it's finally come.

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:53.750
It's time to show off our abilities.

00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:55.730
I wonder what kind of test it will be.

00:15:56.380 --> 00:15:59.300
From this point on, I'm not the one who's going to test you.

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:01.300
They are.

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:12.060
We want you guys to try and get from the goal on one side...

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:14.390
...to the goal on the other.

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:16.690
And we'll be defending it.

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:19.200
Try not to get hurt while you do your best.

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:24.000
"Cry 'Havoc,' and let slip the dogs of war,"

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:27.530
Shakespeare, Julius Caesar.

00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:31.100
Who's going to go first? Who's going to go first?

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:32.910
You go first, Arisa.

00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:34.600
I don't want to.

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:36.690
We don't know how they're going to move.

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:38.440
I'm going.

00:16:38.860 --> 00:16:39.300
Eh?

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:43.290
Whoa, Kouta's really getting into this!

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:45.540
It's the opposite, I'm sure.

00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:46.760
Go!

00:16:59.100 --> 00:16:59.970
Who's next?

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:01.630
Masaru Odawara!

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:11.950
Oh, that can't be!

00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:14.600
Even if he said to feel it...

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:18.720
I mean, I'm going to compete in manipulator art...

00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:22.080
That's no good, Arisa.

00:17:22.300 --> 00:17:24.290
I'm sure if you moved like this over there...

00:17:26.490 --> 00:17:26.920
Go!

00:17:27.570 --> 00:17:28.860
Go go go!

00:17:29.090 --> 00:17:30.390
Oh, a feint.

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:32.940
Hmm, so it's that kind of movement...

00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:36.270
But the Bianca would be better for tight turns...

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:37.330
This can't be!

00:17:37.980 --> 00:17:39.500
Do your best! What's wrong?

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:41.240
Speed up right there...

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:42.130
Ugh...

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:46.410
Damn it!

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:52.090
Hmm... at this rate, we won't be able to breach that defense...

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:52.710
Next!

00:17:52.790 --> 00:17:54.280
The Big Four really are impressive.

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:57.200
I wonder if they're feeling the universe.

00:17:57.700 --> 00:17:59.600
It's your turn, Katase.

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:01.690
Huh? Me?

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:08.470
But, Miss Leila, I don't have any interest in astroball...

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:09.460
Don't dawdle!

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:10.380
Yes, ma'am!

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:14.740
It looks like that girl is the last one.

00:18:15.130 --> 00:18:16.580
So this was all for nothing, huh?

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:20.450
The best one today was the one that got past the half line.

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:21.430
All right, then...

00:18:21.690 --> 00:18:22.100
Go!

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:26.290
Even if you say that, I still haven't finished my analysis!

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:28.980
Is she getting cold feet?

00:18:29.430 --> 00:18:31.180
In that case, I'll push her out.

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.100
Hmm... um...

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:43.120
I don't understand, so I'll just go!

00:18:48.650 --> 00:18:49.710
She just dodged Ayaka.

00:18:49.950 --> 00:18:51.710
She's doing some pretty tricky stuff, isn't she?

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:52.340
Let's go!

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:05.120
Huh? Shipon has cut off most of her automatic controls.

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:08.770
What? You're still monitoring Shipon?

00:19:09.550 --> 00:19:11.340
Only because her machine is still customized.

00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:14.700
Oh, she just turned off her positioning system.

00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:20.100
You have to feel the universe, Shima-chan.

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:24.990
I don't understand the universe! I don't even know where the goal is!

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:28.580
Damn, for her to double back here!

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:30.880
Not bad, Katase!

00:19:35.590 --> 00:19:36.420
Oh! The goal!

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:37.620
Wait!

00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:43.430
For THAT Katase to fly like that...

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:47.870
It's the goal!

00:19:48.470 --> 00:19:49.450
I won't let you through!

00:19:57.430 --> 00:19:58.070
She did it!

00:19:58.160 --> 00:19:58.710
Shipon!

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:20.160
It's kind of a mysterious feeling...

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:27.640
Shipon, that was incredible, that was incredible!

00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:29.730
Yeah, it was incredible.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:32.770
It was surprising to be shown that kind of maneuverability.

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:35.600
What happened, Shipon?

00:20:36.050 --> 00:20:38.990
I wonder if I felt the universe.

00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:40.820
What nonsense are you talking about?

00:20:40.890 --> 00:20:43.790
You've seen the universe tons of times up until now.

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:46.190
That's not what I mean...

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:54.460
It's the Big Four.

00:20:58.820 --> 00:20:59.920
You got us.

00:21:00.390 --> 00:21:03.040
We will allow you to be the fifth player.

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:04.080
Whoa!

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:07.210
It's frustrating, but I've got to admit that you're it.

00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:10.280
Shipon's an astroball player.

00:21:10.360 --> 00:21:12.380
Um, but I...

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:13.430
Now!

00:21:15.280 --> 00:21:16.620
Now you, too.

00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:19.490
But, but I'm...

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:22.130
What are you doing, Shipon? Hurry.

00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:23.490
Touch!

00:21:24.620 --> 00:21:26.090
Victory for the Stellvia!

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:27.570
Victory!

00:21:28.060 --> 00:21:30.460
Um, um, I...

00:21:30.750 --> 00:21:33.270
Leave the customization of your Bianca to me!

00:21:33.340 --> 00:21:35.070
What color do you want for the coloring?

00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:36.840
Horns, let's put on horns!

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:37.460
Hm.

00:21:37.780 --> 00:21:41.310
I can't believe that THAT girl is going to play astroball.

00:21:42.050 --> 00:21:43.470
Glory to the Stellvia!

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:44.790
Glory!

00:21:45.590 --> 00:21:49.540
Am I not allowed to participate in manipulator art?

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:47.140
Glory

00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:49.860
Glory to the Stellvia!

00:21:49.860 --> 00:21:51.520
Glory to the Stellvia!
Um...

00:21:51.600 --> 00:21:52.670
Glory!

00:21:55.360 --> 00:22:00.890
Atashi wa itsumo sora wo Hikaru sora wo miageteta

00:21:55.360 --> 00:22:00.890
I was always looking up at the sky, the sparkling sky

00:21:55.360 --> 00:22:00.890
あたしはいつも空を 光る空を見上げてた

00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:07.570
Tabitatsu tsubasa te ni ire Kono sora mioroshite mitai no

00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:07.570
I'll obtain wings to take off because I want to look down at this sky

00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:07.570
飛び立つ翼手に入れ この空見下ろしてみたいの

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:15.330
Mirai wa dou agaitete mo Kanarazu otozureru kara

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:15.330
Even with how I'm struggling, I'll certainly visit the future

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:15.330
未来はどうあがいてても 必ず訪れるから

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:21.240
Dare mo mita koto no nai keshiki wo Nozonde shimau

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:21.240
I'm wishing for scenery that no one has seen

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:21.240
誰も見たことのない景色を 望んでしまう

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:29.020
Todomaru koto wo shiranai Fuan wo kakaeta yume wo

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:29.020
I don't know about things that stay put, or dreams that hold onto anxiety

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:29.020
とどまる事を知らない 不安を抱えた夢を

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:35.940
Ima wa kokoro omomuku mama ni dakou

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:35.940
Now let's embrace the proceeding spirit

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:35.940
今は心赴くままに抱こう

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:42.730
Naite warau tabi ni omou Atashi ga ikiteru imi wo

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:42.730
I cry every time I think you smile, I'll live for the meaning of it

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:42.730
泣いて笑う度に思う あたしが生きてる意味を

00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:51.900
Hito wa maru de Irotoridori no hoshi no you da ne

00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:51.900
People are completely multicolored like the stars, you know?

00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:51.900
人はまるで 色とりどりの星のようだね

00:22:52.510 --> 00:22:58.950
Kazaritateta you na kirei na yozora

00:22:52.510 --> 00:22:58.950
The beautifully decked out night sky

00:22:52.510 --> 00:22:58.950
飾り立てたような綺麗な夜空

00:22:59.170 --> 00:23:04.860
Soshite mata Atashi wa miageta

00:22:59.170 --> 00:23:04.860
And still I looked up

00:22:59.170 --> 00:23:04.860
そしてまた あたしは見上げた・・・

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:07.030
Next episode

00:23:05.880 --> 00:23:07.300
Hello, this is Shima.

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:08.340
This is Arisa!

00:23:08.640 --> 00:23:10.970
Oh, I hate this.

00:23:11.480 --> 00:23:15.540
Why do I have to become an astroball player?

00:23:12.410 --> 00:23:15.680
In any case, Shipon has become an astroball regular!

00:23:15.750 --> 00:23:17.440
By the way, what kind of competition is astroball?

00:23:17.520 --> 00:23:19.610
All right, please explain it in an easy to understand, compact manner!

00:23:19.680 --> 00:23:24.310
I think it's like lacrosse or basketball, something like that.

00:23:24.390 --> 00:23:25.620
It's a battle with the competition!

00:23:25.620 --> 00:23:25.890
What?

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:27.630
And a mysterious beautiful girl appears!

00:23:27.590 --> 00:23:27.860
What?

00:23:27.860 --> 00:23:30.540
The next episode of Stellvia of the Universe...

00:23:30.570 --> 00:23:31.490
"I Won't Lose"!

00:23:31.580 --> 00:23:32.740
Please look forward to it!

00:23:32.050 --> 00:23:35.050
Episode Six:
I Won't Lose
